    6
  ],
  "rules": [
    "GPIO are 3.3 V only. 5V on any IO pin kills the chip.",
    "GPIO8 and GPIO9 are strapping pins: nothing external may pull GPIO8 low or GPIO9 low during reset.",
    "GPIO12/13 are the USB link; reconfiguring them disconnects the board.",
    "Eyes run on 5V with 3.3V data (works, but at the edge of SK6812 VIH); keep the data line short.",
    "Total 3V3 load including Wi-Fi peaks (~350 mA) must stay under 600 mA.",
    "The -1U module has no PCB antenna: Wi-Fi/BLE need an antenna on U.FL.",
    "PWR LED D3 can be disabled by cutting solder jumper JP1 on the back."
  ],
